there's barely any pickups,

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:32.020
there are rooms that you go into,

00:29:32.020 --> 00:29:34.100
to fight smaller batches of enemies,

00:29:34.260 --> 00:29:35.200
to acquire pickups,

00:29:35.380 --> 00:29:37.180
but for the most part, this is the game.

00:29:37.340 --> 00:29:38.800
I wanted to ask you guys,

00:29:39.020 --> 00:29:40.820
just from a setting,

00:29:41.320 --> 00:29:42.840
and, you know,

00:29:42.920 --> 00:29:44.700
thematic storytelling point of view,

00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:46.700
what'd you think of the actual,

00:29:46.860 --> 00:29:49.180
like, stages, and the progression of the story?

00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:50.900
Did it feel movie-like,

00:29:51.040 --> 00:29:52.460
and that it was getting bigger,

00:29:52.640 --> 00:29:55.180
or, was it just the same,

00:29:55.440 --> 00:29:56.740
you know, the same scenery,

00:29:56.760 --> 00:29:57.880
over and over again?

00:29:58.180 --> 00:30:00.640
I mean, I think that the little,

00:30:00.640 --> 00:30:02.840
cut scenes that are played between,

00:30:03.360 --> 00:30:04.220
each level,

00:30:04.420 --> 00:30:05.280
were, were charming.

00:30:05.540 --> 00:30:06.500
It's very 80s,

00:30:06.560 --> 00:30:08.400
it's very, action movie.

00:30:09.640 --> 00:30:11.140
I wouldn't say that it's,

00:30:11.420 --> 00:30:13.060
all that, engaging,

00:30:13.360 --> 00:30:15.040
in terms of like, what's gonna happen next,

00:30:15.160 --> 00:30:16.940
like, obviously you're going to win.

00:30:19.220 --> 00:30:22.360
But, I think there is some,

00:30:22.820 --> 00:30:23.720
there's some good, like,

00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:24.680
level variety, like,

00:30:24.760 --> 00:30:27.000
I mean, it's not entirely unique,

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.360
there's a jungle level,

00:30:28.520 --> 00:30:30.360
a prison level,

00:30:30.600 --> 00:30:32.100
a, I guess,

00:30:32.280 --> 00:30:34.920
like a, industrial level,

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:36.980
but there's enough,

00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:38.060
that it doesn't feel like,

00:30:38.280 --> 00:30:39.480
everything is the same,

00:30:39.740 --> 00:30:41.620
it's just, we've seen it all before,

00:30:41.660 --> 00:30:43.080
in some other context.

00:30:43.380 --> 00:30:44.580
There is something weird here,

00:30:44.700 --> 00:30:45.660
though, about beat-em-ups,

00:30:45.780 --> 00:30:46.640
for me personally,

00:30:46.880 --> 00:30:48.220
that, we spend so much time,

00:30:48.360 --> 00:30:50.100
talking about the combat, but in a game like,

00:30:50.100 --> 00:30:51.240
Ninja Gaiden,

00:30:51.580 --> 00:30:53.320
we would have talked about the combat,

00:30:53.540 --> 00:30:54.420
and then we would have talked about,

00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:57.780
so many other, aspects of the same game too,

00:30:58.380 --> 00:30:59.980
and beat-em-ups are just like,

00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:03.000
one, very honed in,

00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:04.020
focused part,

00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:05.180
of what essentially,

00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:06.880
every NES platformer,

00:31:06.880 --> 00:31:08.180
can also offer you.

00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:09.660
So, for me,

00:31:09.920 --> 00:31:11.200
what made Double Dragon,

00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:12.880
stand out, was the,

00:31:13.560 --> 00:31:14.600
destructible environments,

00:31:14.860 --> 00:31:16.880
and being able to like, pick up objects,

00:31:17.120 --> 00:31:18.520
that you found, and stuff.

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:20.380
Here, you know,

00:31:20.660 --> 00:31:22.560
other than like, picking up a knife,

00:31:22.720 --> 00:31:24.080
that they, had in their hands,

00:31:24.140 --> 00:31:25.140
that if you punch them, and they,

00:31:25.300 --> 00:31:26.720
they're lucky enough to drop it,

00:31:26.880 --> 00:31:28.200
you can pick up that knife. Otherwise,

00:31:28.520 --> 00:31:29.380
there's not like,

00:31:30.340 --> 00:31:31.200
there's not a lot of,

00:31:31.780 --> 00:31:32.920
interactability, or even,

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:33.960
Well, there is one thing,

00:31:34.560 --> 00:31:35.580
like, go for it. So,

00:31:35.860 --> 00:31:37.060
one thing that I would say,

00:31:37.180 --> 00:31:38.720
that POW does,

00:31:38.900 --> 00:31:40.480
to remove itself,

00:31:40.720 --> 00:31:42.560
from just being a cookie cutter,

00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:45.260
beat-em-up,

00:31:45.420 --> 00:31:46.320
is that,

00:31:46.500 --> 00:31:47.420
throughout each level,

00:31:47.480 --> 00:31:48.700
you're going to find,

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:50.680
these little optional caves,

00:31:50.980 --> 00:31:53.240
or, shipping containers,

00:31:53.540 --> 00:31:55.600
or whatever, contextually they are,

00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:56.980
but these little nooks,

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:58.260
that you can move off into,

00:31:58.820 --> 00:32:01.260
that at the, once you clear that space,

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:02.500
you will get a power-up,

00:32:02.540 --> 00:32:03.780
and, you're obviously,

00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:06.220
sort of, trading off the risk,

00:32:06.400 --> 00:32:07.620
of losing HP,

00:32:07.840 --> 00:32:09.140
or even losing a life,

00:32:09.180 --> 00:32:10.100
by going into them,

00:32:10.160 --> 00:32:12.540
because you're fighting, an optional mob,

00:32:13.160 --> 00:32:15.000
um, for the reward,

00:32:15.320 --> 00:32:16.640
of either like, brass knuckles,

00:32:16.860 --> 00:32:19.220
or, an armor vest,

00:32:19.420 --> 00:32:21.480
or, whatever the third thing is,

00:32:21.980 --> 00:32:23.460
um, and,

00:32:23.600 --> 00:32:24.840
these all have,

00:32:25.280 --> 00:32:26.440
very, uh,

00:32:26.840 --> 00:32:28.700
useful, attributes to them,

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:30.120
uh, and,

00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:31.840
I, I think that, that does,

00:32:31.840 --> 00:32:32.660
make it unique,

00:32:32.680 --> 00:32:33.700
in at least one way,

00:32:34.520 --> 00:32:35.360
no, and that's true,

00:32:35.440 --> 00:32:36.520
because that wasn't in,

00:32:36.540 --> 00:32:37.560
the arcade version,

00:32:37.860 --> 00:32:39.780
yeah, and,

00:32:39.820 --> 00:32:41.100
and those things, like,

00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:42.840
I think it's really,

00:32:43.300 --> 00:32:44.920
uh, it's a well done,

00:32:45.200 --> 00:32:46.020
risk versus reward,

00:32:46.160 --> 00:32:47.340
because those, some of those rooms,

00:32:47.460 --> 00:32:48.400
are very difficult,

00:32:48.960 --> 00:32:50.080
but those power-ups,

00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:52.300
are, are worth it,

00:32:52.780 --> 00:32:54.300
like, if you can, if you can come out,

00:32:54.320 --> 00:32:56.020
with the armor, like,

00:32:56.060 --> 00:32:57.100
that means any projectile,

00:32:57.140 --> 00:32:58.160
will just bounce off of you,

00:32:58.200 --> 00:32:59.200
for the rest of the level, or,

00:32:59.340 --> 00:33:00.220
or when you lose your life,

00:33:00.220 --> 00:33:01.500
like, that's really,

00:33:01.500 --> 00:33:02.460
that's really powerful,

00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:03.560
but it feels like a perfect,

00:33:03.820 --> 00:33:05.060
it's not like overpower,

00:33:05.540 --> 00:33:07.260
overpowered, because it's only projectile weapons,

00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:08.960
and it feels like a perfect balance,

00:33:09.100 --> 00:33:11.100
of like, it really does make me think,

00:33:11.120 --> 00:33:12.000
when I come across those,

00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:13.820
like, there's some tough enemies,

00:33:14.040 --> 00:33:16.040
in those sometimes, in those little nooks,

00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:17.840
um, so like,

00:33:17.900 --> 00:33:19.200
I have to kind of decide,

00:33:19.480 --> 00:33:20.360
on the fly, like,

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:21.320
how worth it is,

00:33:21.760 --> 00:33:22.840
is this, um,

00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:26.580
you know, is this armor, and it's not always a no-brainer,

00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:27.960
which I think is, is a great thing,

00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:29.340
for, for a game like this.

00:33:45.060 --> 00:33:47.040
on the arcade side,

00:33:47.280 --> 00:33:49.160
uh, if I did play the arcade game,

00:33:49.260 --> 00:33:50.560
because I heard good things about it,

